<title>FINLAND: FINNISH JAN-MAY ADVERTISING UP 7.5 PCT YR/YR-STUDY.</title>
<headline>FINNISH JAN-MAY ADVERTISING UP 7.5 PCT YR/YR-STUDY.</headline>
<dateline>HELSINKI 1997-07-03</dateline>
<text>
<p>Estimated advertising spending</p>
<p>in Finland rose 7.5 percent year-on-year to 2.09 billion markka</p>
<p>in January-May, research firm Gallup-Mainostieto said in a</p>
<p>report received on Thursday.</p>
<p>Newspaper advertising, clearly the biggest sector, rose 4.0</p>
<p>percent to 1.20 billion markka, it said.</p>
<p>Television advertising rose 10.8 percent year-on-year in</p>
<p>January-May to 486.7 million markka, and commercial television</p>
<p>station MTV3 -- merging with media group Aamulehti --</p>
<p>had 467.6 million markka of this for a 96 percent market share.</p>
<p>It gave the following figures:</p>
<p>			    January-May	yr/yr change</p>
<p>			    (FIM million)    (percent)</p>
<p> NEWSPAPERS		1,199.5		 +4.0</p>
<p> MTV3			  467.6		+11.2</p>
<p> PTV4			   19.0		 +1.2</p>
<p> TOTAL TELEVISION	  486.7		+10.8</p>
<p> Public magazines	  150.8		+17.9</p>
<p> Specialist magazines    109.7		+21.5</p>
<p> Client magazines	   21.4		+15.1</p>
<p> TOTAL PERIODICALS	 281.9		+19.0</p>
<p> RADIO			  58.9		 +7.2</p>
<p> BILLBOARDS		   61.0		 +4.8</p>
<p> CINEMA			  2.8		 +2.7</p>
<p> TOTAL ADVERTISING     2,090.8		 +7.5</p>
<p>NOTE - PTV4 television station is owned by the privately</p>
<p>held Sanoma group and started broadcasting nationwide in June as</p>
<p>Neloskanava, the second national commercial channel. State TV</p>
<p>YLE is non-commercial.</p>
<p>-- Helsinki newsroom +358-9-680 50 245, news@reuters.fi</p>
</text>
